# ============================================================================
# Image copy/src-over kernel SPIR-V
# Push constants: rx,ry,dst_w,dst_h,fb_w,fb_h,clip x/y/w/h,enabled,
#                 opacity,mode,src_w,src_h
# Bindings: fb (set=0,binding=0), src (set=0,binding=1)
# ============================================================================

fn spirv_blit() -> [u8]:
    """Real SPIR-V compute kernel for checked image copy and src-over.

    Mode 0 copies nearest-neighbor ARGB pixels (exact when source and
    destination dimensions match). Mode 1 applies clip and opacity then
    straight-ARGB Porter-Duff src-over with Engine2D integer truncation.
    Dispatch: 2D, LocalSize 16x16.

    2026-08-08: src-over channel unpremultiply divides by the computed
    out_a (sa + (dst_a*inv)/255), matching color.spl's CPU `blend()`. It
    previously divided by the constant 255, which silently agreed with
    the CPU path only when the destination pixel's alpha byte was 255;
    for any other destination alpha the two backends produced different
    RGB — see doc/08_tracking/bug/host_2d_vulkan_and_simd_spec_reds_2026-08-08.md
    item 1. Regenerated via spirv-dis/spirv-as (spirv-val clean).

    2026-09-12: these words are no longer hand-assembled. They are
    glslangValidator output for the GLSL that `_glsl_blit()` returns in
    backend_vulkan_glsl.spl, produced by scripts/tool/gen-blit-spirv.shs and
    pinned byte-for-byte by scripts/check/check-blit-spirv-pinned.shs. The
    hand-patch path is what let the GLSL text keep the OLD pre-unpremultiply
    formula (out_r = (s*sa + d*inv)/255 -> 0x101F2F3F) while the blob carried
    the frozen CPU formula (0x101E2D3C) with nothing able to notice. See
    doc/08_tracking/bug/vulkan_glsl_blend_formula_stale_vs_cpu_2026-09-12.md.
    Do NOT edit the bytes below by hand -- edit the GLSL and regenerate.
    """
